## Context

The catalogue/manifest currently resolve latest retrieval by source ID. Assertion evidence needs exact historical acquisition, edition, extraction and saved bytes; old coverage and failed searches must survive.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

Acquire changed bytes from the same URL plus a mirror, repeated timestamp and failed attempt. The old assertion must still resolve to its original hash; each attempt remains distinct and mirrors do not become independent support.

## Actions

Crosswalk existing sources, manifest, project-source links, claims and pilot acquisition tables into source revisions/attempts/editions/extractions/evidence. Inventory authority coverage, project coverage, dry searches, news leads and country observations for preserved ownership. Retain unknown admission times and origin roles; legacy attempts have no invented sweep IDs. Produce idempotent migration manifests and unresolved-evidence reports. Reuse DVC objects and harvester with compatibility for exact existing headers.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every input row has a retained mapping or explicit disposition
- [ ] Exact evidence tuples resolve to available bytes or explicit unresolved status
- [ ] Source refresh cannot redirect old assertions or manufacture historical knowledge
- [ ] Coverage/search attempts and primary-secondary uncertainty remain recoverable
- [ ] Same-input rerun preserves identities and output hashes

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

